t":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"kg","note":null},{"ingredientId":"chorizo","rawName":"Chorizo","rawMeasure":"4","amount":4.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"morcilla","rawName":"Morcilla","rawMeasure":"2","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"salt","rawName":"Salt","rawMeasure":"To taste","amount":null,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"To taste"}],"steps":["Prepare the Fire: Start a wood fire in your grill and let it burn down to coals.","Season the Meat: Generously salt the beef cuts.","Grill the Meat: Place the beef on the grill, starting with the thickest cuts farthest from the coals. Add chorizo and morcilla after the beef has been cooking for a while.","Cook to Perfection: Cook the meat, turning occasionally, until it reaches your desired doneness. Typically, ribs may take up to 2 hours; thinner cuts will cook faster.","Rest and Serve: Let the meat rest for about 10 minutes before slicing. Serve with chimichurri sauce and grilled vegetables.","Pro Tips:.","Use a mix of wood and charcoal for a consistent heat source. Wood adds flavor, while charcoal maintains temperature.","Season the meat just before grilling to ensure it retains its moisture and flavor.","Serving Suggestions:.","Serve with a side of chimichurri sauce, a fresh tomato salad, and crusty bread. Pair with a robust Malbec wine to complement the rich flavors of the meat."],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"53133","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/53133","originalUrl":"https://www.munchery.com/blog/the-ten-iconic-dishes-of-argentina-and-how-to-cook-them-at-home/"}},{"id":"mdb-53069","title":"Bistek","cuisine":"Filipino","mealTypes":["main"],"flavor":{"salty":4,"sweet":1,"sour":3,"bitter":0,"umami":4,"spicy":0},"textures":["saucy","tender"],"moods":["comfort","hearty"],"servings":4,"prepMinutes":70,"cookMinutes":30,"difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"beef","rawName":"Beef","rawMeasure":"1 lb","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"lb","note":null},{"ingredientId":"soy_sauce","rawName":"Soy Sauce","rawMeasure":"5 tablespoons","amount":5.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"lemon","rawName":"Lemon","rawMeasure":"1","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"garlic","rawName":"Garlic","rawMeasure":"3 cloves","amount":3.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"clove","note":null},{"ingredientId":"onion","rawName":"Onion","rawMeasure":"3 parts","amount":3.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"parts"},{"ingredientId":"olive_oil","rawName":"Olive Oil","rawMeasure":"4 tbs","amount":4.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"water","rawName":"Water","rawMeasure":"1 cup","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"cup","note":null},{"ingredientId":"salt","rawName":"Salt","rawMeasure":"1 pinch","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"pinch","note":null}],"steps":["Marinate beef in soy sauce, lemon (or calamansi), and ground black pepper for at least 1 hour. Note: marinate overnight for best result.","Heat the cooking oil in a pan then pan-fry half of the onions until the texture becomes soft. Set aside.","Drain the marinade from the beef. Set it aside. Pan-fry the beef on the same pan where the onions were fried for 1 minute per side. Remove from the pan. Set aside.","Add more oil if needed. Saute garlic and remaining raw onions until onion softens.","Pour the remaining marinade and water. Bring to a boil.","Add beef. Cover the pan and simmer until the meat is tender. Note: Add water as needed.","Season with ground black pepper and salt as needed. Top with pan-fried onions.","Transfer to a serving plate. Serve hot. Share and Enjoy!"],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"53069","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/53069","originalUrl":"https://panlasangpinoy.com/bistek-tagalog-beefsteak-recipe/"}},{"id":"mdb-53199","title":"Thai beef stir-fry","cuisine":"Thai","mealTypes":["main"],"flavor":{"salty":3,"sweet":1,"sour":0,"bitter":0,"umami":4,"spicy":3},"textures":["saucy","tender"],"moods":["light"],"servings":2,"prepMinutes":10,"cookMinutes":5,"difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"vegetable_oil","rawName":"Vegetable Oil","rawMeasure":"2 tbsp","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"beef","rawName":"Beef","rawMeasure":"400g","amount":400.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"red_chilli","rawName":"Red Chilli","rawMeasure":"1 sliced","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"sliced"},{"ingredientId":"oyster_sauce","rawName":"Oyster Sauce","rawMeasure":"2 tblsp","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"basil","rawName":"Basil Leaves","rawMeasure":"Handful","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"handful","note":null}],"steps":["Heat a wok or large frying pan until smoking hot. Pour in the oil and swirl around the pan, then tip in the beef strips and chilli. Cook, stirring all the time, until the meat is lightly browned, about 3 mins, then pour over the oyster sauce. Cook until heated through and the sauce coats the meat. stir in the basil leaves and serve with plain rice."],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"53199","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/53199","originalUrl":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/thai-beef-stir-fry"}},{"id":"mdb-53076","title":"Bread omelette","cuisine":"Indian","mealTypes":["breakfast","snack"],"flavor":{"salty":2,"sweet":0,"sour":0,"bitter":0,"umami":2,"spicy":0},"textures":["fluffy"],"moods":["comfort","light"],"servings":1,"prepMinutes":5,"cookMinutes":5,"difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"bread","rawName":"Bread","rawMeasure":"2","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"egg","rawName":"Egg","rawMeasure":"2","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"salt","rawName":"Salt","rawMeasure":"0.5","amount":0.5,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null}],"steps":["Make and enjoy."],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"53076","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/53076","originalUrl":null}},{"id":"mdb-52831","title":"Chicken Karaage","cuisine":"Japanese","mealTypes":["main","snack"],"flavor":{"salty":3,"sweet":1,"sour":1,"bitter":0,"umami":4,"spicy":0},"textures":["crispy","tender"],"moods":["comfort","indulgent"],"servings":4,"prepMinutes":70,"cookMinutes":20,"difficulty":"medium","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"chicken","rawName":"Chicken","rawMeasure":"450 grams Boneless skin","amount":450.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":"boneless skin"},{"ingredientId":"ginger","rawName":"Ginger","rawMeasure":"1 tablespoon","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"garlic","rawName":"Garlic","rawMeasure":"1 clove","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"clove","note":null},{"ingredientId":"soy_sauce","rawName":"Soy sauce","rawMeasure":"2 tablespoons","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"sake","rawName":"Sake","rawMeasure":"1 tablespoon","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"sugar","rawName":"Granulated sugar","rawMeasure":"2 teaspoon","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"potato_starch","rawName":"Potato starch","rawMeasure":"1/3 cup","amount":0.333,"amountMax":null,"unit":"cup","note":null},{"ingredientId":"vegetable_oil","rawName":"Vegetable oil","rawMeasure":"1/3 cup","amount":0.333,"amountMax":null,"unit":"cup","note":null},{"ingredientId":"lemon","rawName":"Lemon","rawMeasure":"1/3 cup","amount":0.333,"amountMax":null,"unit":"cup","note":null}],"steps":["Add the ginger, garlic, soy sauce, sake and sugar to a bowl and whisk to combine. Add the chicken, then stir to coat evenly. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour.","Add 1 inch of vegetable oil to a heavy bottomed pot and heat until the oil reaches 360 degrees F. Line a wire rack with 2 sheets of paper towels and get your tongs out. Put the potato starch in a bowl.","Add a handful of chicken to the potato starch and toss to coat each piece evenly.","Fry the karaage in batches until the exterior is a medium brown and the chicken is cooked through. Transfer the fried chicken to the paper towel lined rack. If you want the karaage to stay crispy longer, you can fry the chicken a second time, until it's a darker color after it's cooled off once. Serve with lemon wedges."],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"52831","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/52831","originalUrl":"https://norecipes.com/karaage-recipe"}},{"id":"mdb-52791","title":"Eton Mess","cuisine":"British","mealTypes":["dessert"],"flavor":{"salty":0,"sweet":5,"sour":2,"bitter":0,"umami":0,"spicy":0},"textures":["creamy","crunchy"],"moods":["fresh","indulgent"],"servings":4,"prepMinutes":15,"cookMinutes":0,"difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"strawberries","rawName":"strawberries","rawMeasure":"500g","amount":500.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"double_cream","rawName":"double cream","rawMeasure":"400ml","amount":400.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"ml","note":null},{"ingredientId":"meringue_nests","rawName":"meringue nests","rawMeasure":"3 x 7.5cm","amount":3.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"x 7.5cm"},{"ingredientId":"ginger_cordial","rawName":"ginger cordial","rawMeasure":"1 tbsp","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"tbsp","note":null},{"ingredientId":"mint","rawName":"Mint","rawMeasure":"sprigs of fresh","amount":1.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"sprig","note":"of fresh"}],"steps":["Purée half the strawberries in a blender. Chop the remaining strawberries, reserving four for decoration.","Whip the double cream until stiff peaks form, then fold in the strawberry purée and crushed meringue. Fold in the chopped strawberries and ginger cordial, if using.","Spoon equal amounts of the mixture into four cold wine glasses. Serve garnished with the remaining strawberries and a sprig of mint."],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"52791","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/52791","originalUrl":null}},{"id":"mdb-53215","title":"Shakshouka","cuisine":"Saudi","mealTypes":["breakfast","main"],"flavor":{"salty":2,"sweet":1,"sour":2,"bitter":0,"umami":3,"spicy":1},"textures":["saucy"],"moods":["comfort"],"servings":2,"prepMinutes":5,"cookMinutes":20,"difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"tomato","rawName":"Tomato","rawMeasure":"250g","amount":250.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"olive_oil","rawName":"Extra Virgin Olive Oil","rawMeasure":"40 ml","amount":40.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"ml","note":null},{"ingredientId":"egg","rawName":"Egg","rawMeasure":"4","amount":4.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"garlic","rawName":"Garlic Clove","rawMeasure":"4 sliced","amount":4.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"sliced"},{"ingredientId":"black_pepper","rawName":"Black Pepper","rawMeasure":"To taste","amount":null,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"To taste"},{"ingredientId":"salt","rawName":"Salt","rawMeasure":"To taste","amount":null,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"To taste"}],"steps":["First, pan fry the black pepper and garlic over a dry medium heat until fragrant.","Add a good amount of extra virgin olive oil and infuse for a minute.","Once the oil heats up, add the tomatoes and salt, and cover with a lid. Simmer for 5 minutes.","Remove the lid and mash the tomatoes. Reduce until you reach the desired consistency of choice.","Make craters for the eggs and lower the heat. Carefully crack the eggs into the craters, making sure it touches the pan and not the tomato sauce.","Cover the eggs and leave it for 5 minutes without lifting the lid.","Remove from the heat and let the residual heat steam the eggs for 1-2 minutes.","Serve with flatbread. Enjoy!"],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"53215","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/53215","originalUrl":"https://cookpad.com/eng/recipes/24999905?ref=search&search_term=saudi+arabia"}},{"id":"mdb-52982","title":"Spaghetti alla Carbonara","cuisine":"Italian","mealTypes":["main"],"flavor":{"salty":4,"sweet":0,"sour":0,"bitter":0,"umami":4,"spicy":0},"textures":["creamy"],"moods":["comfort","indulgent"],"servings":4,"prepMinutes":10,"cookMinutes":15,"difficulty":"medium","ingredients":[{"ingredientId":"spaghetti","rawName":"Spaghetti","rawMeasure":"320g","amount":320.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"egg_yolk","rawName":"Egg Yolks","rawMeasure":"6","amount":6.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":null},{"ingredientId":"salt","rawName":"Salt","rawMeasure":"As required","amount":null,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"As required"},{"ingredientId":"bacon","rawName":"Bacon","rawMeasure":"150g","amount":150.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"pecorino","rawName":"Pecorino","rawMeasure":"50g","amount":50.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"black_pepper","rawName":"Black Pepper","rawMeasure":"As required","amount":null,"amountMax":null,"unit":null,"note":"As required"},{"ingredientId":"butter","rawName":"Butter","rawMeasure":"50g","amount":50.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"parmesan","rawName":"Parmesan","rawMeasure":"50g","amount":50.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"g","note":null},{"ingredientId":"garlic","rawName":"Garlic","rawMeasure":"2 cloves","amount":2.0,"amountMax":null,"unit":"clove","note":null}],"steps":["Put a large saucepan of water on to boil.","Finely chop the 100g pancetta, having first removed any rind. Finely grate 50g pecorino cheese and 50g parmesan and mix them together.","Beat the 3 large eggs in a medium bowl and season with a little freshly grated black pepper. Set everything aside.","Add 1 tsp salt to the boiling water, add 350g spaghetti and when the water comes back to the boil, cook at a constant simmer, covered, for 10 minutes or until al dente (just cooked).","Squash 2 peeled plump garlic cloves with the blade of a knife, just to bruise it.","While the spaghetti is cooking, fry the pancetta with the garlic. Drop 50g unsalted butter into a large frying pan or wok and, as soon as the butter has melted, tip in the pancetta and garlic.","Leave to cook on a medium heat for about 5 minutes, stirring often, until the pancetta is golden and crisp. The garlic has now imparted its flavour, so take it out with a slotted spoon and discard.","Keep the heat under the pancetta on low. When the pasta is ready, lift it from the water with a pasta fork or tongs and put it in the frying pan with the pancetta. Don’t worry if a little water drops in the pan as well (you want this to happen) and don’t throw the pasta water away yet.","Mix most of the cheese in with the eggs, keeping a small handful back for sprinkling over later.","Take the pan of spaghetti and pancetta off the heat. Now quickly pour in the eggs and cheese. Using the tongs or a long fork, lift up the spaghetti so it mixes easily with the egg mixture, which thickens but doesn’t scramble, and everything is coated.","Add extra pasta cooking water to keep it saucy (several tablespoons should do it). You don’t want it wet, just moist. Season with a little salt, if needed.","Use a long-pronged fork to twist the pasta on to the serving plate or bowl. Serve immediately with a little sprinkling of the remaining cheese and a grating of black pepper. If the dish does get a little dry before serving, splash in some more hot pasta water and the glossy sauciness will be revived."],"imageUrl":null,"source":{"name":"TheMealDB","sourceId":"52982","url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/52982","originalUrl":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/ultimate-spaghetti-carbonara-recipe"}}]}